WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.237
Grouping is a good example of why distributed execution changes the performance discussion.

00:00:06.237 --> 00:00:10.072
Logically, group by product is simple.

00:00:10.072 --> 00:00:14.477
We want all rows for the same product summarized together.

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:19.232
Physically, those product rows may be stored on different workers.

00:00:19.232 --> 00:00:23.882
Spark may need to redistribute them before the aggregation can finish.

00:00:23.882 --> 00:00:26.732
So group by changes two things.

00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:31.549
It changes the row grain, and it may also create a data-movement cost.
